## Nano syntax highlighting for PowerShell
## Written by Caleb Denney https://github.com/Denney-tech
##
## Colors follow VS Code's Dark+ theme, with Ansible-style status colors:
## green = true/ok, red = false/error, yellow = warning (see README.md).
## Rules are applied in order, and later rules repaint earlier ones.

## --- Scripts and modules -------------------------------------------------------------------
syntax powershell "\.[pP][sS]([mM])?1$"
header "^#!.*pwsh"
comment "#"

## Parameters: -Path, -Recurse
color #9ab "\B-[[:alpha:]][[:alnum:]_]*"

## Operators: -eq, -like, -match, -and, -f ... (plain, as in VS Code)
icolor normal "\B-[ci]?(eq|ne|gt|ge|lt|le|like|notlike|match|notmatch|contains|notcontains|in|notin|replace|split|is|isnot|as)\>"
icolor normal "\B-(and|or|xor|not|band|bor|bxor|bnot|shl|shr|join|f)\>"

## Numbers: 42, 3.14, 0x1F, 1e3, 10KB
icolor #bca "\<(0x[[:xdigit:]]+|[[:digit:]]+(\.[[:digit:]]+)?(e[+-]?[[:digit:]]+)?)(kb|mb|gb|tb|pb|l|d|u|ul|n|y|s)?\>"

## Declarations
icolor #59d "\<(function|filter|workflow|configuration|param|begin|process|end|clean|dynamicparam|class|enum|using|namespace|module|hidden|static|data)\>"

## Control flow
icolor #c8c "\<(if|elseif|else|switch|foreach|for|while|do|until|break|continue|return|exit|throw|try|catch|finally|trap|in)\>"

## Commands: approved Verb-Noun names (after keywords, so ForEach-Object is one command)
icolor #dda "\<(Add|Approve|Assert|Backup|Block|Build|Checkpoint|Clear|Close|Compare|Complete|Compress|Confirm|Connect|Convert|ConvertFrom|ConvertTo|Copy|Debug|Deny|Deploy|Disable|Disconnect|Dismount|Edit|Enable|Enter|Exit|Expand|Export|Find|ForEach|Format|Get|Grant|Group|Hide|Import|Initialize|Install|Invoke|Join|Limit|Lock|Measure|Merge|Mount|Move|New|Open|Optimize|Out|Ping|Pop|Protect|Publish|Push|Read|Receive|Redo|Register|Remove|Rename|Repair|Request|Reset|Resize|Resolve|Restart|Restore|Resume|Revoke|Save|Search|Select|Send|Set|Show|Skip|Sort|Split|Start|Step|Stop|Submit|Suspend|Switch|Sync|Tee|Test|Trace|Unblock|Undo|Uninstall|Unlock|Unprotect|Unpublish|Unregister|Update|Use|Wait|Watch|Where|Write)-[[:alnum:]_]+\>"

## The name in a function definition
icolor #dda "\<function[[:space:]]+[[:alnum:]_:.-]+"
icolor #59d "\<function\>"

## Types and attributes: [string], [List[int]], [System.IO.File], [Parameter(Mandatory)]
color #4cb "\[[[:alpha:]][[:alnum:]_.]*(\[[[:alnum:]_., ]*\])?\]"
color #4cb "\[[[:alpha:]][[:alnum:]_.]*\("

## Static and instance method calls: [Math]::Round(...), $x.Trim()
color #dda "::[[:alpha:]][[:alnum:]_]*"
color #dda "\.[[:alpha:]][[:alnum:]_]*\("
color normal "\("

## Trailing comments, painted before strings so a "#" inside a string stays string-colored
color italic,#695 "[[:space:]]#.*$"

## Double-quoted strings (variables inside are repainted below, as VS Code does)
color #c97 "\"([^\"`]|`.)*\""

## Variables: $name, $script:name, $env:PATH, ${odd name}, @splat
color #9df "\$[[:alnum:]_?]+(:[[:alnum:]_]+)?"
color #9df "\$\{[^}]*\}"
color #9df "@[[:alpha:]_][[:alnum:]_]*"
## Automatic variables
icolor #4cf "\$(_|args|this|input|PSItem|PSScriptRoot|PSCommandPath|MyInvocation|PSBoundParameters|PSCmdlet|LASTEXITCODE|Error|Host|HOME|PID|PWD|PSVersionTable|ExecutionContext|Matches|IsLinux|IsWindows|IsMacOS)\>"
## Status constants: $true = ok (green), $false = red, $null as a constant
icolor green "\$true\>"
icolor red "\$false\>"
icolor #59d "\$null\>"

## Single-quoted strings are literal: no variables inside
color #c97 "'([^']|'')*'"

## Whole-line comments (after strings, so commented-out code stays comment-colored),
## #region and #Requires
color italic,#695 "^[[:space:]]*#.*$"
icolor bold,italic,#695 "^[[:space:]]*#(region|endregion)\>.*$"
icolor bold,#c8c "^[[:space:]]*#requires\>.*$"

## Here-strings after line comments, so "# ..." lines inside them stay string-colored
## (variables inside @" "@ show as plain string text)
color #c97 start="@\"$" end="^\"@"
color #c97 start="@'$" end="^'@"

## Block comments after here-strings, so a here-string example inside <# #> (common in
## comment-based help) stays comment-colored. nano can't scope a rule to inside or outside a
## region, so a "<#" inside a here-string starts a comment: rare in real scripts.
color italic,#695 start="<#" end="#>"
icolor bold,italic,#695 "^[[:space:]]*\.(SYNOPSIS|DESCRIPTION|PARAMETER|EXAMPLE|INPUTS|OUTPUTS|NOTES|LINK|COMPONENT|ROLE|FUNCTIONALITY|FORWARDHELPTARGETNAME|FORWARDHELPCATEGORY|REMOTEHELPRUNSPACE|EXTERNALHELP)\>"

## Errors: trailing whitespace
color ,red "[[:space:]]+$"


## --- Data files: module manifests and .psd1 data -------------------------------------------
## A restricted language: hashtables and arrays of literals, so no command or keyword colors.
syntax powershell-data "\.[pP][sS][dD]1$"
comment "#"

## Keys: Name = ...
color #9df "^[[:space:]]*[[:alpha:]_][[:alnum:]_.]*[[:space:]]*="
color normal "="

## Numbers and versions: 0.1.0, 7.4
color #bca "\<[[:digit:]]+(\.[[:digit:]]+)*\>"

## Trailing comments before strings, so a "#" inside a string stays string-colored
color italic,#695 "[[:space:]]#.*$"
## Strings
color #c97 "\"([^\"`]|`.)*\""
color #c97 "'([^']|'')*'"

## The few variables data files allow
icolor green "\$true\>"
icolor red "\$false\>"
icolor #59d "\$null\>"
icolor #4cf "\$(PSScriptRoot|PSCulture|PSUICulture|PSEdition)\>"

## Whole-line comments
color italic,#695 "^[[:space:]]*#.*$"

## Here-strings after line comments, block comments after here-strings (see above)
color #c97 start="@\"$" end="^\"@"
color #c97 start="@'$" end="^'@"
color italic,#695 start="<#" end="#>"

## Errors: trailing whitespace
color ,red "[[:space:]]+$"
